From 0b42305f28915db0a553180cad6dcb9ba86a0d43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 01:45:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] patches/openwrt: disable SMP on lantiq xway

OpenWrt 23.05 reverted SMP on the xway subtarget, but OpenWrt 24.10 has
it enabled again. A FRITZ!Box 7312 (AR9) on OpenWrt 24.10 reboots about
1.6 times per hour, so disable SMP to test this as the cause.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 ...0023-lantiq-xway-disable-SMP-support.patch | 101 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 101 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 patches/openwrt/0023-lantiq-xway-disable-SMP-support.patch

diff --git a/patches/openwrt/0023-lantiq-xway-disable-SMP-support.patch b/patches/openwrt/0023-lantiq-xway-disable-SMP-support.patch
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..e77d8eab
--- /dev/null
+++ b/patches/openwrt/0023-lantiq-xway-disable-SMP-support.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,101 @@
+From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
+Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 01:45:30 +0100
+Subject: lantiq: xway: disable SMP support
+
+OpenWrt 23.05 dropped SMP on the xway subtarget in commit 64d8c277cde0
+("Revert "lantiq: xway: kernel: enable SMP support""). That revert was
+never applied to main, so OpenWrt 24.10 has SMP enabled on xway again.
+
+An AVM FRITZ!Box 7312 (AR9) running kernel 6.6 with SMP enabled reboots
+about 1.6 times per hour. Other FRITZ!Box 7312 on OpenWrt 23.05 without
+SMP stay up for days to months. OpenWrt issue 11397 reports kernel oopses
+on other AR9 devices, which one reporter bisected to the commits enabling
+SMP on xway.
+
+Remove the SMP options from the subtarget config. The cause of the
+reboots is not confirmed yet, so this change also serves as the test.
+
+Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
+
